  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Surface",
      "items": [
        "enqueue(call_record), called once the response has already flushed",
        "Seven /api/v1 routes: prices, unpriced worklist, ceiling, retention, opt-in",
        "price_usage, check_spend_ceiling, get_run_totals — evaluation's three seams",
        "The call-records screen is mounted by prompt-registry, behind prompt.read"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Inside",
      "items": [
        "Six tables in one ledger schema; workspace_id is a value, never a foreign key",
        "A 512-record handoff, then a publisher awaits the confirm off the caller's span",
        "The worker drains a 500-message / 250 ms window, one transaction per workspace",
        "A 256 KB per-body cap: an oversize body is dropped and counted, never truncated"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Guarantees",
      "items": [
        "Metadata is durable, bodies are best-effort — bodies drop first, every drop counted (A-037)",
        "Cost is measured from real usage, priced at the call's own created_at (ADR-0019)",
        "No price row means unpriced with a null cost, never a zero (A-101, BR-07)",
        "outputs: [] — the forbidden edge is call-ledger to anything, and it still holds"
      ]
    }
  ]
